<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Langalibalele</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1814–1889</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Langalibalele was chief of the Hlubi, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nguni">Nguni</a> people of Natal, and was renowned as a rainmaker. In 1873 he refused to have the guns his men had earned at the diamond fields registered, and the Natal government treated this as rebellion, broke up the Hlubi location and exiled him to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robben-island">Robben Island</a>. The affair caused controversy in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, and he was allowed to return to Natal in 1887.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/langalibalele.jpg" alt="Langalibalele" width="320" height="513" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:LL1882_pg008_LANGALIBALELE.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
